{#
    The stand-in checkout (FR-090, FR-091, FR-092).

    Epic-02 owns events and their prices; this screen exists so the workflow behind FR-090 to
    FR-092 can actually be reached — by a person and by a browser test — before there is anything
    with a price to select. It replaces itself the day events land: `ChildCheckout` is the seam,
    and Epic-02's checkout calls the same method with the event's own reference and price.

    The page states plainly that no money moves. `FakePaymentProcessor` is what implements the
    payment port until Epic-05 (FR-097, D-04), and a screen that looked like a real checkout while
    charging nobody would be the more dishonest of the two options.
#}
{% extends 'player/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% form_theme form 'account/_form_theme.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Buy something for {{ player.displayName }}{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}Buy something for {{ player.displayName }}{% endblock %}

{% block player_content %}
    <div class="card">
        <p>
            <strong>Nothing here charges anybody.</strong> Events and payments arrive with later
            releases; this page exists so the approval steps around them work and can be tried.
        </p>
    </div>

    {{ form_start(form) }}
        {{ include('account/_error_summary.html.twig', {form: form}) }}

        {{ form_row(form.purchaseDescription) }}

        <fieldset>
            <legend>{{ form.paymentType.vars.label }}</legend>
            {{ form_widget(form.paymentType) }}
            {{ form_errors(form.paymentType) }}
        </fieldset>

        {{ form_row(form.amount) }}

        <div class="actions">
            <button class="pp-btn pp-btn--primary" type="submit">
                <span aria-hidden="true">Continue to checkout</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">Continue to checkout for {{ player.displayName }}</span>
            </button>
            <a href="{{ path('player_reservations') }}">Cancel</a>
        </div>
    {{ form_end(form) }}
{% endblock %}
